<title>AUSTRALIA: Brambles buys New Zealand CHEP operations.</title>
<headline>Brambles buys New Zealand CHEP operations.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transport group Brambles Industries Ltd said on Tuesday it had acquired 100 percent of the CHEP New Zealand pallet rental business for an undisclosed amount.  </p>
<p>Brambles said the purchase, from Freightways Ltd and the Owens Group Ltd, would result in a more efficient trans-Tasman pallet pool and would be a significant additional revenue source for the pallet division.</p>
<p>The transaction remains conditional on regulatory approval.</p>
<p>Brambles shares closed 30 cents lower at A$26.00 in a generally weaker market.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
